    terms: [["Blessed", "Favoured and happy because of a right relationship with God."], ["Scoffer", "One who mocks wisdom and correction."], ["Path", "A direction of life shaped by many steps."]],
    intro: "Blessed is the man who walks not in the counsel of the wicked, nor stands in the way of sinners, nor sits in the seat of scoffers; but his delight is in the law of the Lord. There is a way that seems right to a man, but its end is the way to death. Everyone who hears these words of mine and does them will be like a wise man who built his house on the rock.",
    context: "The Psalms open with a choice. Proverbs 9 uses two women who each invite the simple to a meal, one leading to life and the other to the grave. Moses told Israel that he set before them life and death, blessing and curse, and urged them to choose life. Jesus ended the Sermon on the Mount with two builders, whose houses stood or fell in the storm. In daily life, most decisions are not dramatic but quietly lead in one direction or the other.",
